# Sahayak — Voice Command Shopping Assistant
# No environment variables are required to run the demo: speech recognition and
# text-to-speech use the browser's built-in Web Speech API, and all data (shopping
# list, history, settings) is persisted to localStorage. This file is provided so the
# data layer can be swapped for a real backend without changing the deployment setup.

# --- Optional: connect a real product catalog / search API later ---
# VITE_PRODUCTS_API_URL=

# --- Optional: connect a hosted NLP/entity-extraction service later ---
# (the app currently ships its own rule-based multilingual NLP layer in
# src/services/nlp/ — no key is needed for that to work)
# VITE_NLP_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: connect a real database (Firebase/Supabase) later ---
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
